## 2. Who is in which analysis

Different questions need different populations. Choosing the wrong one gives numbers that look plausible but answer a different question.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    ALL["All 80,295 players in the extract"]
    ALL --> PRE["16,000 installed May–Dec 2025<br/>99.4% active in 2026 → survivors"]
    ALL --> NEW["64,295 installed 1 Jan – 30 Apr 2026"]

    PRE --> BASE["Active base<br/>DAU · ARPDAU · payer share · Part 2(a) · lapse model"]
    NEW --> BASE

    NEW --> COH["Install cohorts"]
    COH --> R["Retention grid<br/>cell shown only if every player has reached day n"]
    COH --> Q["Jan–Mar installs<br/>full 30 days observed"]
    Q --> CH["Part 3 channels · first purchase · 30-day value"]
    Q --> Q60["Jan–Feb installs<br/>60-day value"]

    ALL --> X["36 anomalous currency accounts"]
    X -. excluded .-> LM["Lapse model"]
```

| Population | Size | Used in | Excluded from |
|---|---:|---|---|
| All players | 80,295 | DAU, ARPDAU, payer share, Part 2(a) | — |
| Pre-2026 installs | 16,000 | Active-base metrics, lapse model | Retention, channels, value per install, first purchase |
| 2026 installs | 64,295 | Retention grid | — |
| Jan–Mar installs | 37,489 | 30-day value, channel comparison | — |
| Jan–Feb installs | 19,280 | 60-day value | — |
| Anomalous currency accounts | 36 | IAP metrics | Lapse model |

Pre-2026 players stay in the active base because they are genuinely active players. They are kept out of anything anchored on install date, because only the ones still playing in 2026 appear in the extract.

