## 4. Data-quality decisions

| Issue | Evidence | Handling |
|---|---|---|
| **`ad_view` timestamps 8 hours ahead** | Ad events span 14:00–07:59 with none 08:00–13:59, while other tables span 06:00–23:59. Raw: 51% of ad player-days have no activity row; shifted −8h: 0%. Raw: 8,212 player-days change cap mid-day; shifted: 0. | All ad analysis uses `ad_view_local`. The 7,732 events dated 1 May on the raw clock are 30 April events and are kept. |
| **Ad data missing 5–6 March** | No ad rows on either day, while activity, purchases and currency spends are normal. | Treated as a logging gap: excluded from ad trends, not counted as zero. |
| **Duplicate purchases** | 122 `purchase_id`s appear twice with the same device, pack and amount. | First occurrence kept in `purchase_clean` (−$1,815.82). |
| **Refunds** | 226 negative rows after de-duplication (−$3,249.74); 222 match an earlier purchase of the same pack by the same player. | Excluded from gross revenue; included in net. |
| **Pre-2026 players are survivors** | 16,000 players installed May–Dec 2025; 99.4% are active in 2026. | Excluded from install-based analysis (section 2). |
| **Purchases with no activity row** | 2,449 of 15,078 gross purchases (16.2%). The share is flat across hours and tiers, so it is not a timezone effect. | Revenue kept. Daily payer share counts only buyers active that day. |
| **Purchases before `install_date`** | 111 purchases by 110 players, a few days before install. | Players kept; time to first purchase clipped to day 0. |
| **`original_device_id` links** | 3,211 links: 94% cross countries, 42% cross platforms. | Not used; each `device_id` is one player. |
| **Anomalous currency spends** | 36 accounts spend up to 75.8M in one event, against balances that never exceed ~17k. | Excluded from the lapse model. No effect on IAP revenue. |
| **Refund rows keep `sale_flag`** | Refunds of sale purchases carry `sale_flag = 1` on non-sale days. | Sale days identified from positive purchases only. |
| **Late first activity** | Only ~65% of new installs are active on their install date. | Retention stays anchored on `install_date`, per the brief; D1 is read with this in mind. |
| **Empty CSV fields** | A plain `LOAD DATA` turns empty fields into `0` / `0000-00-00`. | `setup.sql` loads them as `NULL`. |

### Handling rule

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["Raw tables"] --> B["Flag anomaly"]
    B --> C{"Cause understood?"}
    C -->|Yes| D["Correct in a derived table<br/>(purchase_clean, ad_view_local)"]
    C -->|No| E["Exclude only from the<br/>affected analysis"]
    D --> F["Analysis"]
    E --> F
```

Raw tables are never overwritten; all cleaning lives in derived tables or analysis code.

