## 6. What the data supports, and what it does not

| Supported by the extract | Needs more data or an experiment |
|---|---|
| The ARPDAU drop is explained by tier mix; within-tier change is indistinguishable from zero | Why the mix changed, beyond the observed paid_video ramp |
| Observed 30- and 60-day IAP value per install by tier | Whether any tier is profitable to acquire (needs CPI) |
| No detectable channel difference in value at matched tier mix | Channel differences below ~$0.36–0.45 per install (~20%) |
| Lapse risk can be ranked on unseen weeks | How many lapses an offer prevents (needs a randomised holdout) |
| Players rarely reach the ad cap | The effect of changing the cap (cap assignment method unknown) |
| Revenue dips around each sale; ~78% of the lift is offset | Whether sales add or only move revenue (cadence never varied) |

